cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If DiagHam contributes to your work, please cite it as given under
  preferred-citation. This is the one official DiagHam citation; there are
  no program- or module-specific citation rules. When the DiagHam package
  paper is published it becomes the preferred citation. Stable releases are
  archived on Zenodo (RELEASING.md); where the version you used has a
  Zenodo DOI, cite that version.
title: DiagHam
type: software
abstract: >-
  Exact-diagonalization toolkit for strongly correlated quantum systems:
  fractional quantum Hall effect, fractional Chern and topological
  insulators, Hubbard models, spin chains and quantum dots.
authors:
  - family-names: Regnault
    given-names: Nicolas
  - family-names: Möller
    given-names: Gunnar
  - family-names: Repellin
    given-names: Cécile
  - family-names: Sterdyniak
    given-names: Antoine
  - family-names: Papić
    given-names: Zlatko
  - family-names: Nguyen
    given-names: Duc Phuong
  - family-names: Moran
    given-names: Niall
  - family-names: Wu
    given-names: Yang-Le
license: GPL-2.0-or-later
repository-code: https://github.com/PaulWatford/diagham-cmake-poc
url: https://www.nick-ux.org/diagham/
version: 2026.9.0
date-released: "2026-09-28"
# DiagHam Subversion revision carried: r4493 (scripts_cmake/upstream-revision.txt).
# Zenodo: stable releases are archived there (team decision of 20 October 2026). After the first archived release the
# release maintainer adds its concept DOI under `identifiers:` (RELEASING.md). The licence identifier stays as it is until
# the team decides whether the metadata should say GPL-2.0-only or GPL-2.0-or-later.
keywords:
  - exact diagonalization
  - fractional quantum Hall effect
  - fractional Chern insulators
  - Hubbard model
  - spin chains
preferred-citation:
